MECORD CONNECT — DUAL-USE CONTENT DISCLOSURE

Package: mecord-connect
Publisher: Kinthala Samuel Sampath Kumar
Contact: support@splcart.in

Purpose

mecord-connect is the Windows runtime used to pair a user-authorized computer with Mecord Connect for legitimate development and computer-automation workflows initiated through ChatGPT.

Why this package is declared dual-use

The package contains security-relevant remote-management capabilities because it can:
- connect a local runtime to an authenticated remote relay;
- inspect and modify files within locally authorized project roots;
- expose bounded Git/project operations;
- run locally trusted project commands subject to policy and approval controls;
- interact with browser/UI automation capabilities that are available to the private local runtime but are not broadly exposed by the public plugin.

These capabilities can be useful for legitimate development, administration, automation, support, and security work, but similar capabilities could be misused if operated without authorization. For that reason the package declares:

  "contentPolicy": {
    "class": "dual-use"
  }

Intended legitimate use

The Runtime is intended only for computers, accounts, repositories, websites, data, and services the user owns or is authorized to control.

Safeguards

Mecord Connect is designed to reduce misuse through multiple independent controls, including:
- authenticated OAuth access to the hosted MCP service;
- explicit device pairing and signed device identity;
- locally enforced capability policy and authorized filesystem roots;
- approval requirements for risk-bearing operations;
- restricted public plugin tooling rather than unrestricted terminal/browser/UIA exposure;
- credential/restricted-data guards and minimized public responses;
- fail-closed relay/session behavior;
- ambient credential stripping in the npm launcher;
- immutable source/payload binding, integrity hashes, and Windows-native helper self-tests.

The package is not intended to provide stealth, persistence, credential theft, malware delivery, access-control bypass, or unauthorized surveillance.

Security and abuse reports

Report suspected abuse or security issues privately to support@splcart.in. Do not send live passwords, access tokens, private keys, recovery credentials, or other active secrets.
